{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"885a89dd-9464-4d1f-b671-e1969323cee0","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Challenge Solution: ASIS Arch (Reverse)\n\n#### 🚩 Flag\n```\nASIS{M1ddL3_3nd14n_N1bbL35_M4k3_Q3MU_D122y!}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Summary of Analysis \u0026 Solution\n\n1. **Architecture \u0026 Emulator Reversing**:\n   - `qemu-asisarch` is a custom lightweight emulator implementing **ASISARCH**, a 16-bit RISC VM with 8 general-purpose registers (`r0`–`r7`), 16-bit stack pointer `SP` (starting at `0xFFF0`), program counter `PC` (starting at `0x0000`), and a 64 KB memory space.\n   - Instructions are 32-bit (4 bytes) fixed-length, encoded using position-dependent permutations and rotation/XOR masking parameterized by `PC`.\n   - The VM provides 26 opcodes including custom S-box byte substitution (`0xc2`), memory loads/stores (8-bit and 16-bit), stack operations, bitwise/arithmetic operations, and I/O (`getc`/`putc`).\n\n2. **ROM Verification Pipeline**:\n   - The ROM accepts a 44-byte string (`0x2c`), broken into 22 16-bit little-endian words stored at `0xc000..0xc02a`.\n   - The cipher consists of **10 iterations** of a 3-layer transformation:\n     - **Layer A (Keyed Substitution)**: Each word passes through the bijective 256-byte S-box followed by an XOR with round-dependent keys.\n     - **Layer B (Modular Addition Diffusion)**: Cyclic running cumulative addition with constant `0x5A5A` ($buf[i] \\leftarrow buf[i] + buf[i-1] + 0x5a5a \\pmod{2^{16}}$).\n     - **Layer C (Cellular Linear Diffusion)**: Cellular automaton diffusion with $\\theta(x) = x \\oplus (x \\lll 5) \\oplus (x \\lll 11)$ and a round-dependent rotation shift ($k+1$ for iteration $k$).\n   - Finally, the transformed state is compared against 22 target words derived from `0x7cdb` in the ROM.\n\n3. **Inversion \u0026 Flag Recovery**:\n   - Every layer is algebraically invertible in reverse order ($k = 9 \\dots 0$):\n     - **Inv Layer C**: Inverted by iterating $i = 21 \\dots 0$ with the matching $\\theta$ diffusion.\n     - **Inv Layer B**: Inverted by subtracting adjacent words and constant `0x5A5A` from $i = 21 \\dots 1$, then updating index $0$.\n     - **Inv Layer A**: Inverted by XORing with the round keys and looking up the inverse S-box table.\n   - Inverting the 10 rounds from the target values directly recovers the 44-byte flag.\n\n---\n\n### 📁 Generated Files\n- Reusable solver script: [`solver/solve.py`](file:///home/light/Workspace/CTF/ASIS_CTF_2026/Reverse/ASIS_Arch/solver/solve.py)\n- Saved flag: [`flag.txt`](file:///home/light/Workspace/CTF/ASIS_CTF_2026/Reverse/ASIS_Arch/flag.txt)\n- Full technical writeup: [`writeup/README.md`](file:///home/light/Workspace/CTF/ASIS_CTF_2026/Reverse/ASIS_Arch/writeup/README.md)\n- Local verification report: [`script/worker-report.json`](file:///home/light/Workspace/CTF/ASIS_CTF_2026/Reverse/ASIS_Arch/script/worker-report.json)\n","duration_seconds":417.374221147,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":817959,"output_tokens":76214,"thinking_tokens":28217,"cache_read_tokens":5794258,"total_tokens":894173}}}
